IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `vmu-nouns`
IMPORT `vmu-time`

-- Sections 6 and 7: notice of the values before 1 June, and the calculation of a fee or a penalty from the number of units.
-- The date arithmetic and the roundings are in vmu-time; this module says which instruments each rule reaches and what the notice must contain.

§ `Section 6 -- Notification of values of fee and penalty units`

-- "Before 1 June in each year the Treasurer must publish in the Government Gazette and in a newspaper circulating generally throughout Victoria notice of
-- (a) the value of the fee unit ...; and (b) the value of the penalty unit ...". All four facts are needed: both publications before 1 June, in a newspaper
-- that circulates generally throughout Victoria, with the notice stating both values for the financial year commencing on 1 July in that year.
-- src:67 | Before 1 June in each year the Treasurer must publish in the Government Gazette and in a newspaper circulating generally throughout Victoria notice of—
-- src:68 | (a) the value of the fee unit that is to apply for the financial year commencing on 1 July in that year; and
-- src:69 | (b) the value of the penalty unit that is to apply for the financial year commencing on 1 July in that year.
@ref s 6, s 6(a), s 6(b) (src:67-69)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `the day on which notice is published in the Government Gazette` IS A DATE
      `the day on which notice is published in a newspaper` IS A DATE
      `the newspaper circulates generally throughout Victoria` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the value of the fee unit that is to apply for the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the value of the penalty unit that is to apply for the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 6 -- the Treasurer has published the notice that section 6 requires` MEANS
        `s 6 -- notice is published in the Gazette and in a newspaper before 1 June in the year` year `the day on which notice is published in the Government Gazette` `the day on which notice is published in a newspaper`
    AND `the newspaper circulates generally throughout Victoria`
    AND `the notice states the value of the fee unit that is to apply for the financial year`
    AND `the notice states the value of the penalty unit that is to apply for the financial year`

§ `Section 7 -- Calculation of a fee or penalty`

-- "The amount of a fee provided for by an Act, a statutory rule or a legislative instrument by a fee unit is to be calculated by multiplying ...".
-- The section names those three kinds of instrument; for any other kind the text gives no rule, so NOTHING.
-- src:73 | (1) The amount of a fee provided for by an Act, a statutory rule or a legislative instrument by a fee unit is to be calculated by multiplying the number of fee units applicable by the value of a fee unit fixed under section 5.
@ref s 7(1) (src:73)
GIVEN `where the fee is provided for by a fee unit` IS AN Instrument
      `the number of fee units applicable` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of a fee unit fixed under section 5` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 7(1) -- the amount of the fee, where the instrument is one the subsection names` MEANS
    CONSIDER `where the fee is provided for by a fee unit`
    WHEN `an Act` THEN JUST `amount`
    WHEN `a statutory rule` THEN JUST `amount`
    WHEN `a legislative instrument` THEN JUST `amount`
    WHEN `an instrument of another kind` THEN NOTHING
    WHERE
        `amount` MEANS `s 7(1) -- the amount of a fee, in dollars` `the number of fee units applicable` `the value of a fee unit fixed under section 5`

-- "The amount of a penalty provided for by an Act or statutory rule by a penalty unit": a legislative instrument is not named, so NOTHING for it.
-- src:74 | (2) The amount of a penalty provided for by an Act or statutory rule by a penalty unit is to be calculated by multiplying the number of penalty units applicable by the value of a penalty unit fixed under section 5.
@ref s 7(2) (src:74)
GIVEN `where the penalty is provided for by a penalty unit` IS AN Instrument
      `the number of penalty units applicable` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of a penalty unit fixed under section 5` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 7(2) -- the amount of the penalty, where the instrument is one the subsection names` MEANS
    CONSIDER `where the penalty is provided for by a penalty unit`
    WHEN `an Act` THEN JUST `amount`
    WHEN `a statutory rule` THEN JUST `amount`
    WHEN `a legislative instrument` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `an instrument of another kind` THEN NOTHING
    WHERE
        `amount` MEANS `s 7(2) -- the amount of a penalty, in dollars` `the number of penalty units applicable` `the value of a penalty unit fixed under section 5`

-- "may be rounded to the nearest 10 cents": the amount to which the fee calculated under section 7(1) may be rounded.
-- src:75 | (3) The amount of a fee calculated under this section may be rounded to the nearest 10 cents.
@ref s 7(3) (src:75)
GIVEN `where the fee is provided for by a fee unit` IS AN Instrument
      `the number of fee units applicable` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of a fee unit fixed under section 5` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 7(3) -- the amount to which the fee calculated under section 7 may be rounded` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 7(1) -- the amount of the fee, where the instrument is one the subsection names` `where the fee is provided for by a fee unit` `the number of fee units applicable` `the value of a fee unit fixed under section 5`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST fee THEN `s 7(3) -- the amount to which the fee may be rounded, to the nearest 10 cents` fee

-- "may be rounded to the nearest dollar": the amount to which the penalty calculated under section 7(2) may be rounded.
-- src:76 | (4) The amount of a penalty calculated under this section may be rounded to the nearest dollar.
@ref s 7(4) (src:76)
GIVEN `where the penalty is provided for by a penalty unit` IS AN Instrument
      `the number of penalty units applicable` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of a penalty unit fixed under section 5` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 7(4) -- the amount to which the penalty calculated under section 7 may be rounded` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 7(2) -- the amount of the penalty, where the instrument is one the subsection names` `where the penalty is provided for by a penalty unit` `the number of penalty units applicable` `the value of a penalty unit fixed under section 5`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST penalty THEN `s 7(4) -- the amount to which the penalty may be rounded, to the nearest dollar` penalty
